        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7-how-they-all-connect",
      "title": "7. How They All Connect",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "All these linked list problems are not separate they are built on a few&nbsp;<strong>core techniques</strong>:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Dummy node</strong>&nbsp;helps simplify edge cases (like head changes).",
            "<strong>Sub-list reversal</strong>&nbsp;is the core idea behind reversing parts or groups.",
            "<strong>Fast/slow pointers</strong>&nbsp;help you find the middle quickly.",
            "<strong>Three-pointer technique</strong>&nbsp;(<code>prev, curr, next</code>) is the base for any reversal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Once you master these, almost every linked list problem starts feeling familiar.",
          "items": []
        },
